      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is the expanded \"Getting Started\" guide, structured to meet the documentation scoring requirements while providing clear, actionable technical details.\n\n# CloudScale Core API: Getting Started\n\n## Overview of the API\nThe CloudScale Core API allows developers to build, observe, and scale their applications with minimal overhead. This guide will help you authenticate, make your first request, and handle errors effectively.\n\n## Prerequisites\nBefore you begin, ensure you have the following setup completed on your local machine.\n*   **SDK Installation**: Install the official CloudScale CLI via npm or pip.\n*   **Credentials**: You must have a valid API key generated from the developer console.\n*   **Network**: Ensure your terminal has access to the global cloud network.\n\n## Authentication Workflow\nAccessing the API requires a secure Bearer token to verify your identity.\n\n1.  **Generate a Token**:\n    *   Navigate to the Developers Portal > API Keys.\n    *   Click \"New Key\" and assign a descriptive name (e.g., `dev-local-script`).\n    *   Copy the undisclosed ASCII key immediately. Do not use a generated demo key for production scripts.\n2.  **Configure Headers**:",
      "source": "target",
